{
 "_comment": "Asset targets for npm run prep-assets: raw/<name>.png -> <dest>. type world = nearest-neighbour + world palette + binary alpha; ui = Lanczos to size x2, soft edges. grid: [cols, rows] splits a sheet into names in reading order ({n} in dest = 1..). fit: contain (default) | fill (stretch, for tiles) | width (scale to the width, keep aspect). trim: false keeps the frame (tiles). palette: false keeps the source colours (textures are tinted by depth in code). variants: extra sizes of the same picture. Any raw tex_<id>.png without an entry goes to world/tex/<id>.png (64x64 tile). crop: [x0,y0,x1,y1] fractions cut before trimming. straighten: shift each column up so the top edge is flat. tile: flatten the painted lighting and make the tile seamless (64x64: the painted textures carry ~68 big pixels across, 32 would alias them into noise). erode: n peels n outer pixel rings (halo left by the backdrop).",
